### Status Card

Create one minimal dark rounded status card containing exactly two rows.

#### Month Row

Render:

- small calendar outline icon using the accent color
- text exactly: `{{ challenge.month_label }}`

Emphasize the current month number using the accent color.

Render the total number with lower visual emphasis or reduced opacity.

#### MRR Row

Below one thin divider, render:

- small coin or currency outline icon
- text exactly: `Current MRR: {{ content.revenue_label }}`

Emphasize `{{ content.revenue_label }}` using the accent color.

Do NOT add any other information inside this card.

Specifically, do not add:

- start date
- deadline
- calendar month name
- current-period labels
- progress percentage
- target MRR
- secondary statistics

### Progress Bar

At the bottom of the banner, render one long horizontal progress bar.

Start label:

`{{ challenge.start_mrr_formatted }}`

End label:

`{{ challenge.target_mrr_formatted }}`

Progress label:

`{{ revenue.target_progress_percent }}%`

The visual fill length and circular marker position must correspond to exactly {{ revenue.target_progress_percent }}% of the distance from the starting value to the target value.

Place the percentage immediately below the progress marker.

When progress is very small, keep the percentage slightly to the right of the starting label so both labels remain readable.

Never center the percentage on the full track unless the actual progress position requires it.

Do not draw any revenue history chart.

## Layout

Follow this approximate composition.

### Left Main Region

Use approximately 58–62% of the usable banner width.

Arrange vertically:

1. top label
2. main headline
3. subtitle
4. apps section

Use generous negative space around the headline.

Do not turn the entire left region into a dashboard.

### Header Hierarchy

Use approximately this visual hierarchy:

- top label: small
- headline: very large, bold, condensed or semi-condensed
- subtitle: medium
- apps section label: small to medium
- app information: compact

The headline should visually dominate all other elements.

### Apps Region

Keep the app section compact and easy to scan.

Preferred visual structure for each app:

`[APP ICON]  App Name    MRR`

Underneath:

`[Store icon] amount   |   [Store icon] amount`

Do not put individual apps inside separate large cards.

{% if apps and apps|length <= 3 %}

Place every app block on a **single horizontal row** beneath the apps section label.

Use the unused width between the left content and the status card — do not leave a tall empty column by stacking apps vertically.

Keep even horizontal spacing between app blocks.

{% elif apps %}

Prefer a horizontal row of app blocks. Wrap to a second row only if a single row would become cramped.

{% else %}

(No apps section.)

{% endif %}

### Right Status Region

Use approximately 28–32% of the usable banner width.

Place the status card toward the right side of the banner.

Vertically center it relative to the main information area.

The card should feel secondary to the main headline.

Do not make it oversized.

### Bottom Progress Region

Use almost the full usable banner width.

The progress bar should:

- span horizontally across the banner
- remain visually simple
- have comfortable padding above and below
- leave enough space beneath it for its labels
{% if watermark.enabled and watermark.position == "bottom_center" %}
- leave the bottom-center attribution reservation unobstructed
{% elif watermark.enabled and watermark.position == "top_right" %}
- leave the top-right attribution reservation unobstructed
{% endif %}

## Progress Bar Style

Use:

- capsule or pill-shaped track
- rounded ends
- dark translucent track
- subtle low-contrast border
- filled section using a smooth accent-to-primary gradient
- circular marker at the fill edge
- thin light outline around the marker
- optional subtle tick marks

Do not use:

- stacked bars
- line charts
- revenue charts
- legends
- fake data points
- axes

{% if apps %}

## App Icon Chroma Markers

Real app icons will be composited programmatically after generation.

For each app, create exactly one chroma marker.

Marker requirements:

- target size: approximately 48 × 48 px
- acceptable range: 42–52 px
- rounded square
- approximately 12 px corner radius (~25% of marker size; must match post-process mask)
- fill exactly {{ icon_marker_hex }}
- if {{ icon_marker_hex }} is `#FF0000`, use RGB exactly `(255, 0, 0)`
- completely flat solid fill
- no gradient
- no border
- no shadow
- no glow
- no texture
- no icon
- no glyph
- no lettering
- no artwork inside the marker

Keep at least approximately 8 px of non-red space around every marker.

The marker must remain fully visible and unobstructed.

Do not place:

- text over it
- decorative lines over it
- glow over it
- borders over it
- UI elements over it

Pure {{ icon_marker_hex }} must not appear anywhere else in the generated image.

{% endif %}

## Store Icons

App Store and Play Store icons are NOT post-processed.

They must be drawn directly in the generated banner.

For each app:

- draw one small recognizable App Store icon beside the App Store MRR amount
- draw one small recognizable Play Store icon beside the Play Store MRR amount
- target approximately 14–20 px visual size
- keep them clean and immediately recognizable
- use them as compact platform indicators

Do not use chroma markers for store icons.

Do not write the platform names as text.

